<h3 data-start=3D"3812" data-end=3D"3866" class=3D"">Explication d=C3=A9tai=
ll=C3=A9e de chaque dossier et fichier</h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"3868" data-end=3D"3900" class=3D"">1. <strong data-start=
=3D"3876" data-end=3D"3900">Dossier <code data-start=3D"3886" data-end=3D"3=
898">myproject/</code></strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"3904" data-end=3D"3978" class=3D"">Ce dossier contient les=
 fichiers de configuration globaux de votre projet.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3983" data-end=3D"4815">
<li data-start=3D"3983" data-end=3D"4815" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3985" data-end=3D"4215" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
985" data-end=3D"4000"><code data-start=3D"3987" data-end=3D"3998">settings=
/</code></strong> : Plut=C3=B4t que de stocker toutes les configurations da=
ns un seul fichier <code data-start=3D"4072" data-end=3D"4085">settings.py<=
/code>, il est recommand=C3=A9 de les diviser en plusieurs fichiers pour mi=
eux g=C3=A9rer les environnements. La structure typique pourrait =C3=AAtre =
:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4221" data-end=3D"4815">
<li data-start=3D"4221" data-end=3D"4368" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4223" data-end=3D"4368" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
223" data-end=3D"4236"><code data-start=3D"4225" data-end=3D"4234">base.py<=
/code></strong> : Contient les configurations de base communes =C3=A0 tous =
les environnements (ex. : <code data-start=3D"4317" data-end=3D"4333">INSTA=
LLED_APPS</code>, <code data-start=3D"4335" data-end=3D"4347">MIDDLEWARE</c=
ode>, <code data-start=3D"4349" data-end=3D"4360">DATABASES</code>, etc.).<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4374" data-end=3D"4516" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4376" data-end=3D"4516" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
376" data-end=3D"4396"><code data-start=3D"4378" data-end=3D"4394">developm=
ent.py</code></strong> : Contient les param=C3=A8tres sp=C3=A9cifiques au d=
=C3=A9veloppement (ex. : <code data-start=3D"4459" data-end=3D"4473">DEBUG =
=3D True</code>, <code data-start=3D"4475" data-end=3D"4486">DATABASES</cod=
e> pour un environnement local).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4522" data-end=3D"4690" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4524" data-end=3D"4690" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
524" data-end=3D"4543"><code data-start=3D"4526" data-end=3D"4541">producti=
on.py</code></strong> : Contient les param=C3=A8tres pour un environnement =
de production (ex. : <code data-start=3D"4613" data-end=3D"4628">DEBUG =3D =
False</code>, configurations pour la base de donn=C3=A9es en production, et=
c.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4696" data-end=3D"4809" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4698" data-end=3D"4809" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
698" data-end=3D"4714"><code data-start=3D"4700" data-end=3D"4712">testing.=
py</code></strong> : Param=C3=A8tres sp=C3=A9cifiques pour les tests (ex. :=
 configurations de base de donn=C3=A9es temporaires).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4819" data-end=3D"4943" class=3D"">Cette approche permet d=
e maintenir une configuration centralis=C3=A9e tout en g=C3=A9rant diff=C3=
=A9rents environnements de mani=C3=A8re propre.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"4945" data-end=3D"4972" class=3D"">2. <strong data-start=
=3D"4953" data-end=3D"4972">Dossier <code data-start=3D"4963" data-end=3D"4=
970">apps/</code></strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"4976" data-end=3D"5155" class=3D"">Ce dossier contient tou=
tes les applications de votre projet. Un projet Django est constitu=C3=A9 d=
e plusieurs applications qui peuvent =C3=AAtre ind=C3=A9pendantes, r=C3=A9u=
tilisables, et =C3=A9volutives.</p>
<p data-start=3D"5160" data-end=3D"5291" class=3D"">Chaque application peut=
 avoir sa propre logique m=C3=A9tier et ses propres composants (mod=C3=A8le=
s, vues, contr=C3=B4leurs, tests). Par exemple :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5295" data-end=3D"5491">
<li data-start=3D"5295" data-end=3D"5382" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5297" data-end=3D"5382" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
297" data-end=3D"5308"><code data-start=3D"5299" data-end=3D"5306">core/</c=
ode></strong> : L'application centrale qui g=C3=A8re la logique m=C3=A9tier=
 principale du projet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5386" data-end=3D"5491" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5388" data-end=3D"5491" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
388" data-end=3D"5400"><code data-start=3D"5390" data-end=3D"5398">users/</=
code></strong> : L'application g=C3=A9rant l'authentification des utilisate=
urs (inscription, connexion, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5496" data-end=3D"5556" class=3D"">Pour chaque application=
, vous trouverez des fichiers comme :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5560" data-end=3D"5896">
<li data-start=3D"5560" data-end=3D"5612" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5562" data-end=3D"5612" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
562" data-end=3D"5577"><code data-start=3D"5564" data-end=3D"5575">models.p=
y</code></strong> : Contient les mod=C3=A8les de donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5616" data-end=3D"5681" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5618" data-end=3D"5681" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
618" data-end=3D"5632"><code data-start=3D"5620" data-end=3D"5630">views.py=
</code></strong> : Contient la logique des vues de l'application.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5685" data-end=3D"5739" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5687" data-end=3D"5739" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
687" data-end=3D"5700"><code data-start=3D"5689" data-end=3D"5698">urls.py<=
/code></strong> : D=C3=A9finit les routes de l'application.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5743" data-end=3D"5825" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5745" data-end=3D"5825" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
745" data-end=3D"5759"><code data-start=3D"5747" data-end=3D"5757">admin.py=
</code></strong> : Permet de personnaliser l'interface d'administration de =
Django.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5829" data-end=3D"5896" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5831" data-end=3D"5896" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
831" data-end=3D"5845"><code data-start=3D"5833" data-end=3D"5843">tests.py=
</code></strong> : Contient les tests unitaires pour l=E2=80=99application.=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"5898" data-end=3D"5927" class=3D"">3. <strong data-start=
=3D"5906" data-end=3D"5927">Dossier <code data-start=3D"5916" data-end=3D"5=
925">static/</code></strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"5931" data-end=3D"6184" class=3D"">Ce dossier contient tou=
s les fichiers statiques (images, fichiers CSS, JavaScript) utilis=C3=A9s d=
ans le projet. Django servira ces fichiers en production lorsque la configu=
ration sera correctement mise en place (utilisation de <code data-start=3D"=
6154" data-end=3D"6182">django.contrib.staticfiles</code>).</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6189" data-end=3D"6293">
<li data-start=3D"6189" data-end=3D"6217" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6191" data-end=3D"6217" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
191" data-end=3D"6201"><code data-start=3D"6193" data-end=3D"6199">css/</co=
de></strong> : Fichiers CSS.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6221" data-end=3D"6254" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6223" data-end=3D"6254" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
223" data-end=3D"6232"><code data-start=3D"6225" data-end=3D"6230">js/</cod=
e></strong> : Scripts JavaScript.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6258" data-end=3D"6293" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6260" data-end=3D"6293" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
260" data-end=3D"6273"><code data-start=3D"6262" data-end=3D"6271">images/<=
/code></strong> : Images du projet.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"6295" data-end=3D"6327" class=3D"">4. <strong data-start=
=3D"6303" data-end=3D"6327">Dossier <code data-start=3D"6313" data-end=3D"6=
325">templates/</code></strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"6331" data-end=3D"6526" class=3D"">Ce dossier contient tou=
s les templates HTML utilis=C3=A9s par votre projet. Il est conseill=C3=A9 =
de garder tous les fichiers de template organis=C3=A9s dans des sous-dossie=
rs par application ou fonctionnalit=C3=A9.</p>
<p data-start=3D"6531" data-end=3D"6540" class=3D"">Exemple :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6544" data-end=3D"6737">
<li data-start=3D"6544" data-end=3D"6614" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6546" data-end=3D"6614" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
546" data-end=3D"6561"><code data-start=3D"6548" data-end=3D"6559">base.htm=
l</code></strong> : Le template de base utilis=C3=A9 pour les autres pages.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6618" data-end=3D"6737" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6620" data-end=3D"6737" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
620" data-end=3D"6632"><code data-start=3D"6622" data-end=3D"6630">users/</=
code></strong> : Dossier contenant les templates pour les pages li=C3=A9es =
aux utilisateurs (<code data-start=3D"6706" data-end=3D"6718">login.html</c=
ode>, <code data-start=3D"6720" data-end=3D"6735">register.html</code>).</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"6739" data-end=3D"6767" class=3D"">5. <strong data-start=
=3D"6747" data-end=3D"6767">Dossier <code data-start=3D"6757" data-end=3D"6=
765">media/</code></strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"6771" data-end=3D"6958" class=3D"">Ce dossier est utilis=
=C3=A9 pour stocker les fichiers t=C3=A9l=C3=A9charg=C3=A9s par les utilisa=
teurs (ex. : images de profil, fichiers PDF, etc.). Il est important de le =
diff=C3=A9rencier des fichiers statiques.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"6960" data-end=3D"6988" class=3D"">6. <strong data-start=
=3D"6968" data-end=3D"6988">Dossier <code data-start=3D"6978" data-end=3D"6=
986">tests/</code></strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"6992" data-end=3D"7251" class=3D"">Ce dossier peut conteni=
r des tests unitaires globaux pour le projet, en dehors des tests sp=C3=A9c=
ifiques =C3=A0 chaque application. Il peut =C3=AAtre utile pour organiser l=
es tests d'int=C3=A9gration ou de fonctionnalit=C3=A9 qui ne sont pas direc=
tement li=C3=A9s =C3=A0 une seule application.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"7253" data-end=3D"7286" class=3D"">7. <strong data-start=
=3D"7261" data-end=3D"7286">Fichiers additionnels</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"7290" data-end=3D"7680">
<li data-start=3D"7290" data-end=3D"7428" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7292" data-end=3D"7428" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
292" data-end=3D"7314"><code data-start=3D"7294" data-end=3D"7312">requirem=
ents.txt</code></strong> : Liste des d=C3=A9pendances Python n=C3=A9cessair=
es au projet. Il permet de g=C3=A9rer facilement les biblioth=C3=A8ques ave=
c <code data-start=3D"7422" data-end=3D"7427">pip</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7432" data-end=3D"7561" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7434" data-end=3D"7561" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
434" data-end=3D"7450"><code data-start=3D"7436" data-end=3D"7448">Dockerfi=
le</code></strong> : Si vous utilisez Docker pour conteneuriser votre appli=
cation, ce fichier d=C3=A9crit l'environnement d'ex=C3=A9cution.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7565" data-end=3D"7680" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7567" data-end=3D"7680" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
